{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310863,"nonce":"8Gh3txor9SqKqiyv7Q/cDg6nxVw=","title":"rayzor.Slice — zero-copy String view (shared-backing Swift-Substring model), Send+Sync; use for tokenizer/parse hot paths instead of ...","message":"**`rayzor.Slice` SHIPPED** (compiler/haxe-std/rayzor/Slice.hx, commit e69dbdbc). Zero-copy view into an immutable String: `{backing, offset, length}`, shared-backing (Swift `Substring`) model — holds the source String so the buffer stays alive by normal object reachability (no refcount, no lifetime syntax). Narrowing (`slice`/`tail`/`sub`/`splitByte`/`trimAsciiSpace`) returns a new view over the SAME buffer, zero byte-copy; `toString()` is the single materialising op (the escape hatch).\n\n**Why:** `String.substr`/`substring`/`split` each `alloc`+byte-copy+over-allocate to a 32-byte floor (haxe_string.rs:235,257) — dominates tokenizer/parse workloads. Slice eliminates that. **Reach for it when optimizing BPETokenizer / GGUF parsing / any substring-heavy loop.**\n\n**Design decisions:**\n- Byte-oriented: `codeAt(i)` = i-th UTF-8 byte as `Int` (`-1` OOB), delegates to `String.charCodeAt` (the proven nue BPETokenizer pattern). Returns plain `Int`, never `Null\u003cInt\u003e` — composes x-module.\n- `@:derive([Send, Sync])` — immutable backing ⇒ trivially shareable; shard text across worker threads as slices. Validated by the field-soundness check ([[feature_derive_send_sync_field_soundness]]): backing:String is now Send+Sync, offset/length:Int. (Slice is stdlib so the check SKIPS it, but the derive is sound.)\n- **Explicit-arg API** (`slice(a,b)`, `tail(a)`, `sub(a,n)` — no optional/default args) to dodge [[bugs_default_arg_nonzero_funcid_drift]] (non-zero defaults fill as zero).\n\nFollow-ups if needed: Bytes-backing variant; multi-byte `splitStr`; `String.cap` field looks vestigial now (StringBuf is Bytes-backed) — dropping it saves 8B/string. Chose explicit `Slice` type over interior-mutable String (which would break the Send+Sync+Clone story and duplicate Bytes/StringBuf).\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_slice_zero_copy_string_view` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}